meta {
  name: Group service
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  # Group service

  Keys, tokens and the stream index, served by `backend/cmd/groupd`.

  A key travels in a request body and never in a path, a key in a URL being a key in every proxy log between the client and here.
  The index is the exception: a GET has no body a cache or a proxy will honour, so it takes its key in the query.

  Behind the deployment's reverse proxy these routes are paths under the relay's own name, which is why the `Proxied` environment points `groupService` at that name with no port (`deploy/Caddyfile`).
  A relay reached directly has no proxy and therefore no group service, and the app treats that as a machine in no group.
}
